<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Provide.Uterm\Provide.Uterm.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <!--
      No PublishAot / PublishTrimmed here, deliberately.

      They were added for the container image, and an AOT build of this server
      cannot answer a single request. Routes return anonymous types through
      Results.Json, and ASP.NET minimal APIs build their request delegates
      reflectively; AOT has no runtime code generation, so endpoint
      construction throws and every route answers 500 with an empty body:

        System.NotSupportedException: JsonTypeInfo metadata for type
        'Task`1[IResult]' was not provided by TypeInfoResolver of type '[]'

      Worse than useless, it was a trap. The SDK stamps

        "System.Text.Json.JsonSerializer.IsReflectionEnabledByDefault": false

      into uterm.runtimeconfig.json for an ORDINARY build once PublishAot is
      declared, so a plain `dotnet run` produced a server that logged 200 and
      returned 500. That disguised two CI failures as startup and health-check
      problems. `make build-binaries` was unaffected only because it passes the
      no-self-contained flag, which switched these off.

      Reviving AOT is a project, not a flag: 47 anonymous-type responses become
      declared records, all of them need JsonSerializable entries in a
      JsonSerializerContext on the resolver chain, the host moves to
      CreateSlimBuilder, and Shell/Commands.cs stops deserializing JsonElement.
      For a process that starts once and runs for days, the startup win does
      not pay for that. If short-lived CLI startup ever matters, split the CLI
      out of the server assembly and AOT only that.
    -->
    <!-- Ship as lowercase `uterm` (matches Go/Python CLI names). -->
    <AssemblyName>uterm</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
